  {
   "id": 669075,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "<ol class=\"os-raise-noindent\">\n  <li>The number of people with the flu during an epidemic is a function, <span data-math=\"f\">f</span>, of the number of days, <span data-math=\"d\">d</span>, since the epidemic began. The equation <span data-math=\"f(d)=50 \\cdot (\\frac{3}{2})^d\">f(d)=50 \\cdot (\\frac{3}{2})^d</span> defines <span data-math=\"f\">f</span>.\n</li>\n</ol>   <ol class=\"os-raise-noindent\" type=\"a\">\n      <li>How many people had the flu at the beginning of the epidemic?</li>\n    </ol>",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": []
  },
  {
   "id": 669076,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "<ol class=\"os-raise-noindent\" start=\"2\" type=\"a\">\n  <li>What does <span data-math=\"f(1)\">f(1)</span> mean in this situation?</li>\n  </ol>",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1333821,
     "content_html": "The number of people infected after 1 year."
    },
    {
     "id": 1333822,
     "content_html": "The number of people infected grows by a factor of 1."
    },
    {
     "id": 1333823,
     "content_html": "The number of people infected 1 day after the epidemic began."
    },
    {
     "id": 1333824,
     "content_html": "There was 1 year of the epidemic."
    }
